// Integer absolute value is computed in integers.
//
// The runtime exposes one double-precision `nrq_abs`, so an integer argument used
// to be handed to a float parameter unchanged. `abs` now keeps its argument's
// integer type and lowers to a compare-and-negate, while the floating overload
// still goes through the runtime.
int function main() {
    var x = -4;
    print(math.abs(-4));
    print(math.abs(x));
    print(math.abs(-4.5));
    return 0;
}
